# s6_stream_load: checkpoint streamed tensor by tensor; the whole model is never built. Free.
#
# object     owner census at the per-layer peak: 866.5 MB float32 weights in pairs (49 flat vs 49 shaped,
#            1 vs 1): state_dict and module at one instant. Markers: after_model_load 1,150,172 kB, 0.5 s
#            later (layers on disk) 384,688.
# before     x3 (low_cpu_mem_usage=True): duplicate gone, run worse (median 1,337,108 vs x2's 1,194,020;
#            peak moved into conversion).
# lever      safe_open (tensor-wise mmap of model.safetensors) per scope, encoder layers to disk as
#            state_dicts, posix_fadvise(DONTNEED) on faulted pages; three sub-models constructed under
#            torch.random.fork_rng() (init draws would shift the mask stream).
# donor      retired s6_stream_load; its out-of-process shard split (split_safetensors.py) dropped.
# gate       expected byte-identical to s5's.
# expected   ~-30%, 1.0 to 1.1 GB.
SHAFT_SCRIPT=$BASE/bert_perlayer_stream_cpu.py
SHAFT_LEVERS=plaintext_free_cpu,triple_share_free_cpu,trace_nograd_cpu,onnx_single_file_export_cpu,encrypt_spill_cpu
